      "writtenOn": "2017-06-16T21:09:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, a bool value is enough here. The reason that we are using an obj instead a bool value is because in the original design, we want to use the same \"NetworkScanResult\" for all the start/stop/result messages, but in RadioResponse.java, all the errors are wrapped in CommandException, so now the \"scanError\" in NetworkScanResult won\u0027t be used for start/stop messages. Considering there will be on 1 start and 1 stop for each scan, I would recommend keep it as this, at least for ODR.",
